  message: "DONE in PR #2273 (dev 4d49f510e feature + d6395f4d2 manifest). CLOSE CONDITION, point by point.\n(1) ROWS FOR AT LEAST THREE REAL SCHEDULED RUNS, from origin/badges and the merged PRs' manifests. Re-run on dev after the merge: `./scripts/ci-debug trace --ledger full-suite --pipelines taguj/pipelines.jsonl` -> rc 0, 5 rows: pipelines 6550 (passed, range fd5448d16f..fc2d2d8a9c: 49 commits, 12 PR manifests), 6582 (failed: self-tree-validation, test-agent-infra; 31 commits, 7 PRs), 6614 (passed; 36 commits, 8 PRs), and 6480 / 6512, which published no verdict (rows saying so, never clean). Last line: \"selection misses: 0 of 3 run(s) with a verdict and a known range ...; 2 unknown\". Record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/taguj/ (ledger_dev.txt, ledger.json, pipelines.jsonl).\n(2) A TEST FOR THE ROW BUILDER: tests/test_scheduled_trace.py, 6 new tests on throwaway git histories with published verdicts and a stub ci-debug (row per run, PR manifests and what they left out, a run with no verdict, unread logs = unknown, an uncovered line traced into the range, an unreadable range, JSON). Mutations taguj/muts.tsv: 13 planted, 13 red.\nFOUND ON THE WAY AND FIXED IN THE SAME PR: the trace arm charged a PR whose manifest commit did not hold the failing test's file (\"not run by its PR\"). On pipeline 6582 it named PR #2252 for tests/test_kept_work_contexts.py, which PR #2253 added later and whose manifest ran it; the first ledger read 1 miss of 3 because of it. The run now reads as the scheduled environment (the known cause). Also fixed before merge: test files are counted by pytest's python_files patterns at each commit (BRANCHES_*.py had made listed exceed the total), and a PR with two manifest commits is shown once, by its last.\nNOT DONE / NOT ASSERTED: the ledger does not group a PR's commits for the trace arm's \"first manifest at or after\" rule (a commit before a PR's first manifest is judged by that manifest, not the PR's last); 0 of 3 is three runs, not a rate anyone should lean on yet."  # 8a5c
